1. Scope and definitions

"Software" means the original Bones code and documentation made available
under this license by their copyright holders, including the editor,
compiler, runtime, shared packages, and original example code.

"Licensor" means each copyright holder granting rights to their own
contribution under this license. No person grants rights to material they
do not own or have authority to license.

"Editor Service" means a hosted, managed, or remotely accessible offering
that uses, incorporates, or is derived from the Software and gives third
parties access to a substantial set of the Bones editor's authoring
features, such as rigging, animation editing, or animation compilation
and export. This includes access through a user interface or API, and
includes modified, renamed, embedded, and white-label versions.

"Monetized Editor Service" means an Editor Service for which its operator
or an affiliated entity receives or seeks commercial compensation through
paid access, subscriptions, usage fees, advertising, paid feature tiers,
or inclusion in a paid product or service bundle. Calling an offering
free does not exempt it if it is monetized through these means.

