3. Restriction on monetized editor services

You may not operate, offer, sell access to, or distribute the Software as
part of a Monetized Editor Service without separate prior written
permission from the relevant copyright holders.

This restriction applies regardless of modifications, branding,
attribution, delivery architecture, or whether the Software is only one
component of the service. Preserving attribution does not waive this
restriction.

Free Editor Services that are not monetized as defined above are
permitted, subject to the other terms of this license.

4. Commercial games and internal use

You may use the editor and other Software internally, including within a
commercial game studio, and modify them for your workflow.

You may create, publish, sell, and monetize games using the Software,
including through game sales, subscriptions, advertising, and in-game
purchases. You may incorporate, modify, and distribute the Bones runtime
and the shared code required for its operation as part of those games,
including browser, downloadable, and hosted games.

Charging for development work or for games and animations created with
the Software is permitted. These permissions do not allow providing a
Monetized Editor Service to customers or players. A game that uses the
runtime for animation playback does not become an Editor Service merely
because it uses the Software.

